+## P2. Classification — not all overlaps are defects
+
+Full rules and per-name data in `classification.md` / `classification.json`. Categories:
+A exact duplication · B contradiction (same effective context, different value) ·
+C legitimate conditional · D inert conditional · E component-local · F absent compiler
+capability (facet) · G domain token out of place · H explicit temporal compat ·
+I indeterminate. Final label = worst reachable-state category; rendered equality
+(one-level var() resolution) as primary, strict-textual preserved alongside.
+
+| Vertical | Shared | A | B | C | D | E | Notes |
+|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|
+| bithire | 188 | 20 | **42** | 3 | 122 | 1 | 42 B are live in the shipped state; 85 rows carry resolvedEquality UNKNOWN (25 reachable) pending computed styles |
+| evnto | 82 | **79** | 2 | 0 | 1 | 0 | the extension's light block re-states the compiled block nearly wholesale — pure drift surface |
+| rottay | 267 | 0 | 0 | 0 | **267** | 0 | every one carries the F facet: in the shipped state the compiled block does not apply at all |
+
+Two structural discoveries outrank the counts:
+
+1. **The rottay compiled block is a DARK palette emitted under a light-gated selector.**
+   `FIRST_PARTY_ARTIFACT_SPECS` scopes rottay to
+   `html[data-tenant='rottay'][data-theme='light'], .light`
+   (`artifact-renderer/index.ts:65`) while bithire/evnto get unconditional selectors — and
+   180 of the 267 shared compiled values are byte-identical to the extension's
+   DARK-default block (`--ds-sidebar-bg: #0D0D10`, `--ds-modal-bg: #1A1A1E` under a
+   *light* selector). The extension is not rogue here: it supplies the only correct light
+   palette on top of a mislabelled block. NEEDS_OWNER_DECISION: fix the spec selector vs
+   teach the compiler modes — classification is identical either way.
+2. **All three products ship `data-theme="base"`** (registry `theme: 'base'` ×3, no
+   `forceTheme` in any app, provider stamps what resolves), and no selector in any of the
+   six files tests any value other than light/dark. Light and dark are therefore
+   UNREACHABLE-BY-ABSENCE in all product shells — but the showroom reaches both via
+   `forceTheme` today, so every D is observable there and goes live the moment a mode
+   switch ships. D means "inert under current product policy", not "harmless".
+
+Shipped-state defects elevated from the B set (all file:line in `classification.md` §3):
+bithire's entire canvas (`--ds-color-bg-primary` compiled `#F4F8FB` → extension
+`#ffffff`), `--ds-surface-panel` authored gradient → flat fill, muted/disabled ink
+lightened ~2 steps against a now-white ground (contrast re-check required), badge 7px →
+pill, card 12px → 10px, breadcrumb `rem` → `px` (breaks user font scaling), filter-pill
+count ring deleted; and **evnto drops `"Noto Sans Arabic"` from both font-family stacks**
+— a live i18n regression in the shipped state. The bithire "PRODUCTION GUARDRAILS (TOKEN
+REMAP)" section (48 names) is H-ELIGIBLE but NOT H: it cites a reason and WO-UX-05 but
