+## P6. Mandatory single-authority protocol (adopted for every future wave)
+
+No "single source of truth"/"single authority" claim may be certified without
+demonstrating ALL SIX properties separately, each with its own evidence: (1) author
+uniqueness — one authorized declaring location; (2) emitter uniqueness — no second
+compiler/bridge on the channel without explicit coverage; (3) writer uniqueness — no two
+runtime writers per element/channel; (4) precedence correctness — the cascade makes the
+declared owner win; (5) behavioral propagation — editing the canonical source observably
+changes the output (N-2 is the standing counterexample); (6) negative drill — a planted
+second author/emitter/writer makes a guard FAIL. A green gate without its negative drill
+certifies nothing about authority.
+
+Laws: L1 no grep as semantic evidence where an AST exists (the 576-vs-575 delta is the
+standing exhibit); L2 no "duplication" from name intersection without selector/context/
+reachability classification; L3 "generated" is not "single-source" — provenance is
+per-section, not per-file; L4 deterministic output ≠ correct ownership; L5 no total
+without denominator and method; L6 UNKNOWN never becomes PASS; L7 every broad audit
+includes ≥1 full vertical trace source→compiler→artifact→bundle→DOM/computed-style.
+
